[font_size=24][b]Materials and UV Tiles[/b][/font_size]

Each object can contain multiple material slots. Faces choose which slot they use, and each material receives its own UV tile in the full UV Editor.

[font_size=18][b]Add and edit a material[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Select the object.
Add a material slot from the Material section.
Set its name, base colour, metallic value, roughness, and optional albedo texture.
Press Apply Material after changing its properties.
[/ol]

[font_size=18][b]Assign faces to a material[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Enter Face mode.
Select the faces that should use the material.
Choose the required material slot.
Press Assign to Selected Faces.
[/ol]

Only selected faces are reassigned. Other material assignments remain unchanged.

[font_size=18][b]UV layout per material[/b][/font_size]

[ul]
Material slot 1 uses the first tile, material slot 2 uses the second tile, and so on.
The compact UV preview shows only the active material and its texture.
The full UV Editor shows every material tile together.
Unwrap, Smart UV Project, and Pack UV Islands operate only on the active material.
Unwrapping one material does not change the UVs of other materials.
Selecting UVs in another tile makes that material active.
[/ul]

The tiles are an editing layout. Every material still stores ordinary local 0–1 UV coordinates for rendering and export.

[font_size=18][b]Recommended workflow[/b][/font_size]

[ol type=1]
Assign all faces to their intended materials first.
Select one material slot.
Mark seams only on that material's faces where needed.
Unwrap or Smart UV Project that material.
Pack its islands.
Repeat for each remaining material.
Use the texture preview while moving, rotating, or scaling UVs. The 3D model updates during the transform.
[/ol]
